{:edb/db-before-t 572 :edb/db-after-t 573 :edb/tx-data [[13194139533885 50 #inst "2026-10-05T08:17:58.590Z" 13194139533885 true] [17592186179583 1020 #edb/ref 17592186263213 13194139533885 true] [17592186179583 1020 #edb/ref 17592186263255 13194139533885 true] [17592186179583 1020 #edb/ref 17592186263262 13194139533885 true] [17592186179583 1020 #edb/ref 17592186263283 13194139533885 true] [17592186179584 1020 #edb/ref 17592186263220 13194139533885 true] [17592186179584 1020 #edb/ref 17592186263227 13194139533885 true] [17592186179584 1020 #edb/ref 17592186263234 13194139533885 true] [17592186179585 1020 #edb/ref 17592186263241 13194139533885 true] [17592186179585 1020 #edb/ref 17592186263248 13194139533885 true] [17592186179585 1020 #edb/ref 17592186263269 13194139533885 true] [17592186179585 1020 #edb/ref 17592186263276 13194139533885 true] [17592186179995 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533885 true] [17592186179995 1145 "To make our estimation, we proceed as follows:\n\n- We start at $y=56$ on the vertical axis.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13944892/assets/a9d57651c5c342c3d619a20cfae2bc632df47f8924d49f400ed764870b7ae900.png)\n\n- Then, we move right until we intersect the trend line.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13944892/assets/c816d47fc84f31c3a436818777d9473b68e9d8468051c40fe9b7b94005cc89ee.png)\n\n- Finally, we move down until we intersect the horizontal axis.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13944892/assets/e6cbfe34a6e3bd002171d2474542a12c66b7d88ce5989b0fbb4b3542f76a2155.png)\n\nTherefore, the population was $56\\,000$ in approximately the year $2000+10=2010.$" 13194139533885 true] [17592186179996 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533885 true] [17592186179996 1145 "We can estimate the required value by substituting $y=2$ into the equation of the trend line and solving for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-0.5x+9 \\\\ 2 & =-0.5x+9 \\\\ 2+0.5x & =9 \\\\ 0.5x & =7 \\\\ x & =14\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, according to this model, when $y=2$ we have $x≈14.$\n\nNote: The point where $y=2$ is not shown on our trend line. Therefore, our result *may* be unreliable." 13194139533885 true] [17592186179997 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533885 true] [17592186179997 1145 "First, notice that the year $2026$ is $26$ years since the year $2000.$\n\nTo predict the population in $2026,$ we need to substitute $x=26$ into the equation of the trend line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =0.1x+53 \\\\  & =0.1(26)+53 \\\\  & =2.6+53 \\\\  & =55.6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, according to this model, the population will be approximately $55\\,600$ in $2026.$\n\nNote: The point where $x=26$ is not shown on our trend line. Therefore, our result *may* be unreliable." 13194139533885 true] [17592186179999 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139533885 true] [17592186179999 1145 "First, using the hint, let's draw an approximate trend line for our scatter plot.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13944892/assets/5b2ab039994e7c2306cad7e30717fb136b5dfc3a028db284a0e95f49b56d580f.png)\n\nThe trend line passes through $({x}_{1},{y}_{1})=(2,56)$ and $({x}_{2},{y}_{2})=(18,48).$\n\nWe will write the equation of the line in the slope-intercept form \n\n$$\ny=mx+b.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the slope $m$ of the line as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{48-56}{18-2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-8}{16} \\\\  & =-0.5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $m=-0.5$ into the slope-intercept form above, we get\n\n$$\ny=-0.5x+b.\n$$\n\nWe now need to calculate the $y$-intercept $b.$ We can do this by substituting the coordinates of a point on the line. Any point will do, so let's substitute $(2,56):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-0.5x+b \\\\ 56 & =-0.5(2)+b \\\\ 56 & =-1+b \\\\ 57 & =b \\\\ b & =57\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the line is \n\n$$\ny=-0.5x+57.\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute $y=40$ into the equation above and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-0.5x+57 \\\\ 40 & =-0.5x+57 \\\\ 0.5x+40 & =57 \\\\ 0.5x & =17 \\\\ x & =34\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, according to this model, the population will be $40\\,000$ around the year $2000+34=2034.$\n\nNote: The point where $y=40$ is not shown on our trend line. Therefore, our result *may* be unreliable." 13194139533885 true] [17592186263213 1017 #edb/ref 17592186263214 13194139533885 true] [17592186263213 1089 "q-133880" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263213 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533885 true] [17592186263213 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13944892/assets/4de50fc0b2b2f05b9ca60e28ffc65900a2b0780549fbf1cf32150a903a08faf5.png)\n\nThe scatter plot above gives the correspondence between the variables $x$ and $y$ for some data points.\nUse the trend line to predict the value of $x$ when $y=20.$" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263213 1113 #uuid "79babf95-b234-5b7e-a39f-16410ad3c68e" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263213 1145 "To make our prediction, we proceed as follows:\n\n- First, we start at $y=20$ on the $y$-axis.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13944892/assets/ad092e8773bbb8707dc95377b20b29a1f6ddab9e973b0a5fa469e15f47f967cc.png)\n\n- Then, we move right until we intersect the trend line.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13944892/assets/520c396408909577337035a455f5078df148c491ec9d33a75a0f3bbdcaac9a5f.png)\n\n- Finally, we move down until we intersect the $x$-axis.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13944892/assets/67b44784b133813b84204dc63aedf0a07b7edb67a30c52e3dc17d8567fcccb19.png)\n\nTherefore, when $y=20,$ we obtain $x≈7.$" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263214 1000 #edb/ref 17592186263215 13194139533885 true] [17592186263214 1000 #edb/ref 17592186263216 13194139533885 true] [17592186263214 1000 #edb/ref 17592186263217 13194139533885 true] [17592186263214 1000 #edb/ref 17592186263218 13194139533885 true] [17592186263214 1000 #edb/ref 17592186263219 13194139533885 true] [17592186263214 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533885 true] [17592186263214 1041 "selection" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263214 1104 #edb/ref 17592186263217 13194139533885 true] [17592186263214 1110 #uuid "509af303-d6d2-50fa-acaf-4cfc55a200f2" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263215 1034 "3" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263215 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533885 true] [17592186263215 1111 #uuid "0454e4ed-7814-50dd-acdd-31d580709db6" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263216 1034 "8" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263216 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533885 true] [17592186263216 1111 #uuid "2d7346c0-dbae-5a98-966b-6f3f83a444d1" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263217 1034 "7" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263217 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533885 true] [17592186263217 1111 #uuid "b1c11544-7f53-53e1-9402-f897980b249e" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263218 1034 "6" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263218 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533885 true] [17592186263218 1111 #uuid "1839868f-f495-58ec-b509-0cba03d0c0b3" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263219 1034 "4" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263219 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533885 true] [17592186263219 1111 #uuid "6d08db34-747c-5d43-aa8c-8b372dec31ac" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263220 1017 #edb/ref 17592186263221 13194139533885 true] [17592186263220 1089 "q-133884" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263220 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533885 true] [17592186263220 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13944892/assets/e00248d1dd5cb96a5e0099acf5da41913a805dbc388715f0b542aa821a95efa5.png)\n\nThe scatterplot above shows the relationship between the number of hours $x$ a group of people spend watching TV each night and the time $y$ they sleep each night. The equation of the trend line is $y=10-1.25x.$ \n\nAssuming this trend continues, estimate the time a person sleeps per night if they watch TV for $6$ hours." 13194139533885 true] [17592186263220 1113 #uuid "d8fd1d76-7104-56dc-931a-2f7d76cbe576" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263220 1145 "To predict the number of hours a person sleeps after watching TV for $6$ hours, we need to substitute $x=6$ into the equation of the trend line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =10-1.25x \\\\  & =10-1.25(6) \\\\  & =10-7.5 \\\\  & =2.5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, according to this model, a person watching TV for $6$ hours sleeps for approximately $2.5$ hours.\n\nNote: The point where $x=6$ is not shown on our trend line. Therefore, our result *may* be unreliable." 13194139533885 true] [17592186263221 1000 #edb/ref 17592186263222 13194139533885 true] [17592186263221 1000 #edb/ref 17592186263223 13194139533885 true] [17592186263221 1000 #edb/ref 17592186263224 13194139533885 true] [17592186263221 1000 #edb/ref 17592186263225 13194139533885 true] [17592186263221 1000 #edb/ref 17592186263226 13194139533885 true] [17592186263221 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533885 true] [17592186263221 1041 "selection" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263221 1104 #edb/ref 17592186263225 13194139533885 true] [17592186263221 1110 #uuid "ed52e1bf-733c-5819-aed7-8a62be46eed6" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263222 1034 "$2$ hours" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263222 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533885 true] [17592186263222 1111 #uuid "8b9c4cc5-5880-5bbe-9366-370cc2de4c1f" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263223 1034 "$4$ hours" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263223 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533885 true] [17592186263223 1111 #uuid "0692e7e8-7b5e-5fa7-a7d5-480416fae2a2" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263224 1034 "$3$ hours" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263224 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533885 true] [17592186263224 1111 #uuid "319cbfe4-76a5-507f-a440-06c1c95d4f88" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263225 1034 "$2.5$ hours" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263225 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533885 true] [17592186263225 1111 #uuid "c7193e4e-4c5f-590a-b1d5-67e2e5a89970" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263226 1034 "$3.5$ hours" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263226 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533885 true] [17592186263226 1111 #uuid "5c5a6372-6039-5898-99db-1694ca2037c7" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263227 1017 #edb/ref 17592186263228 13194139533885 true] [17592186263227 1089 "q-133928" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263227 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533885 true] [17592186263227 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13944892/assets/91e15117e7797cfce1b94c33d157c2e89fad519c80c715bfc3ef8082c1e38946.png)\n\nThe scatter plot shows the value of a car $y,$ in thousands of dollars, and the number of years $x$ since it was purchased. The equation of the trend line is $y=28-x.$ \n\nAssuming this trend continues, estimate the time it will take for the car to be worth $$20\\,000.$" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263227 1113 #uuid "f68282f1-36e0-5e8b-a38b-3f8d307a758e" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263227 1145 "To predict the number of years it will take for the car to be worth $$20\\,000,$ we need to substitute $y=20$ into the equation of the trend line and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =28-x \\\\ 20 & =28-x \\\\ 20+x & =28 \\\\ x & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, according to this model, it will take approximately $8$ years for the car to be worth $$20\\,000.$\n\nNote: The point where $y=20$ is not shown on our trend line. Therefore, our result *may* be unreliable." 13194139533885 true] [17592186263228 1000 #edb/ref 17592186263229 13194139533885 true] [17592186263228 1000 #edb/ref 17592186263230 13194139533885 true] [17592186263228 1000 #edb/ref 17592186263231 13194139533885 true] [17592186263228 1000 #edb/ref 17592186263232 13194139533885 true] [17592186263228 1000 #edb/ref 17592186263233 13194139533885 true] [17592186263228 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533885 true] [17592186263228 1041 "selection" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263228 1104 #edb/ref 17592186263229 13194139533885 true] [17592186263228 1110 #uuid "ddd772e9-5f18-5103-82cc-ced26dc88acb" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263229 1034 "$8$ years" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263229 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533885 true] [17592186263229 1111 #uuid "bcf59d67-61f0-5167-9bbe-e433b3537a97" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263230 1034 "$9$ years" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263230 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533885 true] [17592186263230 1111 #uuid "7e9db484-acab-5388-a06c-2f082001ce57" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263231 1034 "$10$ years" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263231 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533885 true] [17592186263231 1111 #uuid "0a128075-51d8-547b-9672-aa3bdb33e0f0" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263232 1034 "$7$ years" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263232 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533885 true] [17592186263232 1111 #uuid "493fe5fa-8041-5468-ab9a-a2c8b2e480ed" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263233 1034 "$11$ years" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263233 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533885 true] [17592186263233 1111 #uuid "e8b88070-c610-5498-a9ed-7d64dd99f04e" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263234 1017 #edb/ref 17592186263235 13194139533885 true] [17592186263234 1089 "q-133929" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263234 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533885 true] [17592186263234 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13944892/assets/ce3aec85d418c8f51988f819c04403f3f3ea2e0c0e35165ed729fc1e78d0f12f.png)\n\nThe scatter plot shows the value of an artwork $y,$ in thousands of dollars, and the number of decades $x$ since it was first created. The equation of the trend line is $y=3x+5.$ \n\nAssuming this trend continues, estimate the time it takes for the artwork to be worth $$32\\,000.$" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263234 1113 #uuid "87bad21a-36f4-5e06-9484-4b7826190ce1" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263234 1145 "To predict the time that must pass before the artwork is worth $$32\\,000,$ we need to substitute $y=32$ into the equation of the trend line and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =3x+5 \\\\ 32 & =3x+5 \\\\ 3x & =27 \\\\ x & =9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, according to this model, it takes approximately $9$ decades for the artwork to have a value of $$32\\,000.$ \n\nNote: The point where $y=32$ is not shown on our trend line. Therefore, our result *may* be unreliable." 13194139533885 true] [17592186263235 1000 #edb/ref 17592186263236 13194139533885 true] [17592186263235 1000 #edb/ref 17592186263237 13194139533885 true] [17592186263235 1000 #edb/ref 17592186263238 13194139533885 true] [17592186263235 1000 #edb/ref 17592186263239 13194139533885 true] [17592186263235 1000 #edb/ref 17592186263240 13194139533885 true] [17592186263235 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533885 true] [17592186263235 1041 "selection" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263235 1104 #edb/ref 17592186263240 13194139533885 true] [17592186263235 1110 #uuid "cf0bef1e-0621-57b8-b1f5-0963136b2494" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263236 1034 "$10$ decades" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263236 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533885 true] [17592186263236 1111 #uuid "818c9164-83c7-551d-bcbc-6d1f39c9802a" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263237 1034 "$7$ decades" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263237 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533885 true] [17592186263237 1111 #uuid "6dd2b3a5-8e61-54e1-9c62-a5bbad0c5e5d" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263238 1034 "$11$ decades" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263238 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533885 true] [17592186263238 1111 #uuid "c5852581-47a7-5d89-a02c-c608c93d82bb" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263239 1034 "$8$ decades" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263239 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533885 true] [17592186263239 1111 #uuid "eee37c69-621d-58d1-a6ef-235f80b2e101" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263240 1034 "$9$ decades" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263240 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533885 true] [17592186263240 1111 #uuid "f175c626-c80f-5523-a491-d76b1472d5c8" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263241 1017 #edb/ref 17592186263242 13194139533885 true] [17592186263241 1089 "q-133943" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263241 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533885 true] [17592186263241 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13944892/assets/7ba7aa1cf49bb5a2dc430d9a21baaa8491aa61d8898f2aad142406c5c569b51b.png)\n\nThe scatter plot above gives the correspondence between the variables $x$ and $y$ for some data points. Estimate the value of $x$ when $y=7.$ \n\n*Hint: Assume the trend is linear, and that the trend line passes through the points $(1,1)$ and $(5,4).$*" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263241 1113 #uuid "89b89ff0-333a-5e1a-9504-209847c75169" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263241 1145 "First, using the hint, let's draw an approximate trend line for our scatter plot.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13944892/assets/59efe1b79b0d032179a5210ee694b0d59ad082853ca9fb80a9d79d9f6444f2bf.png)\n\nOur trend line passes through $({x}_{1},{y}_{1})=(1,1)$ and $({x}_{2},{y}_{2})=(5,4).$\n\nWe will write the equation of the line in the slope-intercept form \n\n$$\ny=mx+b.\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the slope $m$ of the line as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4-1}{5-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4} \\\\  & =0.75\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $m=0.75$ into the slope-intercept form above, we get\n\n$$\ny=0.75x+b.\n$$\n\nWe now need to calculate the $y$-intercept $b.$ We can do this by substituting the coordinates of a point on the line. Any point will do, so let's substitute $(1,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =0.75x+b \\\\ 1 & =0.75(1)+b \\\\ 1 & =0.75+b \\\\ b & =0.25\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the line is \n\n$$\ny=0.75x+0.25.\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute $y=7$ into the equation above and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =0.75x+0.25 \\\\ 7 & =0.75x+0.25 \\\\ 6.75 & =0.75x \\\\ x & =9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, according to this model, when $y=7$ we have $x≈9.$\n\nNote: The point where $y=7$ is not shown on our trend line. Therefore, our result *may* be unreliable." 13194139533885 true] [17592186263242 1000 #edb/ref 17592186263243 13194139533885 true] [17592186263242 1000 #edb/ref 17592186263244 13194139533885 true] [17592186263242 1000 #edb/ref 17592186263245 13194139533885 true] [17592186263242 1000 #edb/ref 17592186263246 13194139533885 true] [17592186263242 1000 #edb/ref 17592186263247 13194139533885 true] [17592186263242 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533885 true] [17592186263242 1041 "selection" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263242 1104 #edb/ref 17592186263243 13194139533885 true] [17592186263242 1110 #uuid "18e76129-8164-5989-a81c-797a36d5217d" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263243 1034 "9" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263243 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533885 true] [17592186263243 1111 #uuid "76e5166a-2778-5bb7-96ba-a8cbb31db659" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263244 1034 "9.5" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263244 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533885 true] [17592186263244 1111 #uuid "6c12d04a-0dc5-54ed-b5ce-36e421066103" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263245 1034 "10" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263245 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533885 true] [17592186263245 1111 #uuid "c113465b-8099-5725-8bd8-4d9b28180793" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263246 1034 "8" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263246 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533885 true] [17592186263246 1111 #uuid "831bbf0d-a71d-520a-afc9-096bd17bf9ac" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263247 1034 "8.5" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263247 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533885 true] [17592186263247 1111 #uuid "ac978aa9-c0b4-5e40-b2ce-dd4c0f8a527d" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263248 1017 #edb/ref 17592186263249 13194139533885 true] [17592186263248 1089 "q-133945" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263248 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533885 true] [17592186263248 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13944892/assets/6de719fb9d16173e40759b507f16b0d10cd373059f5d127081d173bc0b3596b1.png)\n\nThe scatter plot above gives the correspondence between the variables $x$ and $y$ for some data points. Estimate the value of $x$ when $y=0.$ \n\n*Hint: Assume the trend is linear, and that the trend line passes through the points $(21,9)$ and $(25,3).$*" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263248 1113 #uuid "8e0da2a3-95bd-5475-bd22-74eac9a023c2" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263248 1145 "First, using the hint, let's draw an approximate trend line for our scatter plot.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13944892/assets/35797fe2923cdf9c741dda57a40401f4759cd722eb748f80d0df960c5d6eef29.png)\n\nOur trend line passes through $({x}_{1},{y}_{1})=(21,9)$ and $({x}_{2},{y}_{2})=(25,3).$\n\nWe will write the equation of the line in the slope-intercept form \n\n$$\ny=mx+b.\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the slope $m$ of the line as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3-9}{25-21} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-6)}{4} \\\\  & =-1.5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $m=-1.5$ into the slope-intercept form above, we get\n\n$$\ny=-1.5x+b.\n$$\n\nWe now need to calculate the $y$-intercept $b.$ We can do this by substituting the coordinates of a point on the line. Any point will do, so let's substitute $(21,9):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-1.5x+b \\\\ 9 & =-1.5(21)+b \\\\ 9 & =-31.5+b \\\\ b & =40.5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the line is \n\n$$\ny=-1.5x+40.5.\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute $y=0$ into the equation above and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-1.5x+40.5 \\\\ 0 & =-1.5x+40.5 \\\\ 1.5x & =40.5 \\\\ x & =27\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, according to this model, when $y=0$ we have $x≈27.$\n\nNote: The point where $y=0$ is not shown on our trend line. Therefore, our result *may* be unreliable." 13194139533885 true] [17592186263249 1000 #edb/ref 17592186263250 13194139533885 true] [17592186263249 1000 #edb/ref 17592186263251 13194139533885 true] [17592186263249 1000 #edb/ref 17592186263252 13194139533885 true] [17592186263249 1000 #edb/ref 17592186263253 13194139533885 true] [17592186263249 1000 #edb/ref 17592186263254 13194139533885 true] [17592186263249 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533885 true] [17592186263249 1041 "selection" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263249 1104 #edb/ref 17592186263254 13194139533885 true] [17592186263249 1110 #uuid "89f65e2c-fa72-599a-879a-c4d8cd3e3175" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263250 1034 "27.5" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263250 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533885 true] [17592186263250 1111 #uuid "06cb7570-0dda-5dd7-bbca-b91721ccd562" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263251 1034 "28" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263251 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533885 true] [17592186263251 1111 #uuid "765183a4-632f-5821-9fe0-f7cb462bac31" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263252 1034 "26.5" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263252 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533885 true] [17592186263252 1111 #uuid "ea338e3a-14ec-55f2-ba91-eb3b9cb42a1e" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263253 1034 "28.5" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263253 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533885 true] [17592186263253 1111 #uuid "e299eee5-ea23-58ba-b8e8-34ea4ee4540d" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263254 1034 "27" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263254 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533885 true] [17592186263254 1111 #uuid "73cfaf92-4d30-5e72-b22