3256 1041 "selection" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263256 1104 #edb/ref 17592186263261 13194139533885 true] [17592186263256 1110 #uuid "36eedd8d-9014-536b-b934-27f97efb12f0" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263257 1034 "$15$ minutes" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263257 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533885 true] [17592186263257 1111 #uuid "750aeaf6-de81-5309-80bf-cb41da17a102" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263258 1034 "$10$ minutes" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263258 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533885 true] [17592186263258 1111 #uuid "23674115-2ade-5706-a0fe-96b4831b77bb" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263259 1034 "$30$ minutes" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263259 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533885 true] [17592186263259 1111 #uuid "28283f1c-d248-50a2-9303-cc7600586f09" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263260 1034 "$25$ minutes" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263260 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533885 true] [17592186263260 1111 #uuid "e8b5f5aa-a75a-5419-acf1-a06330eb4022" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263261 1034 "$20$ minutes" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263261 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533885 true] [17592186263261 1111 #uuid "6da48f8e-8e93-56a8-8417-e73e4079863f" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263262 1017 #edb/ref 17592186263263 13194139533885 true] [17592186263262 1089 "q-133961" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263262 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533885 true] [17592186263262 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13944892/assets/d3d0f871d60b7f7c8280abd7d3eba4337f910bae6b814586b368bbfb0a8dc313.png)\n\nThe scatter plot above shows the weight loss per week (in pounds) vs. the number of hours spent training per week for a group of people. Use the trend line to estimate how much weight a person loses if they train for $4$ hours per week." 13194139533885 true] [17592186263262 1113 #uuid "cbb6ac4c-9e6a-53f5-af48-c57b58c5a491" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263262 1145 "To make our estimation, we proceed as follows:\n\n- We start at $x=4$ on the horizontal axis.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13944892/assets/1e397473de815e2eda88ad33c59e2cf77c336b968ef6a1eeaffa67d9fbc64750.png)\n\n- Then, we move up until we intersect the trend line.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13944892/assets/27c8ce8a7a1feadd4ea16d66f6a283fa245fa737036810924ead4b0148c6d6f5.png)\n\n- Finally, we move left until we intersect the vertical axis.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13944892/assets/a178070d1f62538a35e7e4e363a254c2afa776920079618b80b3bff358601871.png)\n\nTherefore, a person training $4$ hours a week will lose around $3$ pounds of weight." 13194139533885 true] [17592186263263 1000 #edb/ref 17592186263264 13194139533885 true] [17592186263263 1000 #edb/ref 17592186263265 13194139533885 true] [17592186263263 1000 #edb/ref 17592186263266 13194139533885 true] [17592186263263 1000 #edb/ref 17592186263267 13194139533885 true] [17592186263263 1000 #edb/ref 17592186263268 13194139533885 true] [17592186263263 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533885 true] [17592186263263 1041 "selection" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263263 1104 #edb/ref 17592186263268 13194139533885 true] [17592186263263 1110 #uuid "688dc202-b2a1-50fc-a159-751b75a9d7a6" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263264 1034 "$2.5$ pounds" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263264 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533885 true] [17592186263264 1111 #uuid "78799658-f551-5ce6-b7f2-b741208e4045" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263265 1034 "$2$ pounds" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263265 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533885 true] [17592186263265 1111 #uuid "e07c387c-e206-510c-8850-5b6b1b879689" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263266 1034 "$1.5$ pounds" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263266 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533885 true] [17592186263266 1111 #uuid "4d80a4ce-eef0-5f24-865b-20991a0fd478" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263267 1034 "$4$ pounds" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263267 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533885 true] [17592186263267 1111 #uuid "d918b1d8-5d42-58df-9b12-f88cf8a92b1a" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263268 1034 "$3$ pounds" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263268 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533885 true] [17592186263268 1111 #uuid "c021ddcb-1e80-547e-aa39-dec005173694" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263269 1017 #edb/ref 17592186263270 13194139533885 true] [17592186263269 1089 "q-133964" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263269 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139533885 true] [17592186263269 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13944892/assets/032c895f40d741c8468c531d96c763943a391cf7033ca4a63407d6b7b36bacef.png)\n\nThe scatter plot shows the value of a motorcycle, in thousands of dollars, several years after it was purchased. Assuming this trend continues, estimate the motorcycle's value $10$ years after it was purchased.\n\n*Hint: Assume the trend is linear and that the trend line passes through the points $(2,5)$ and $(4,4).$*" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263269 1113 #uuid "6261a08b-e81a-5e2c-ae24-27b897291587" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263269 1145 "First, using the hint, let's draw an approximate trend line for our scatter plot.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13944892/assets/145a6a57bcd24c99e7de73f470de61c673b10f5a0d88b0c64527a17e52a0dc86.png)\n\nThe trend line passes through $({x}_{1},{y}_{1})=(2,5)$ and $({x}_{2},{y}_{2})=(4,4).$\n\nWe will write the equation of the line in the slope-intercept form \n\n$$\ny=mx+b.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the slope $m$ of the line as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4-5}{4-2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-1)}{2} \\\\  & =-0.5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $m=-0.5$ into the slope-intercept form above, we get\n\n$$\ny=-0.5x+b.\n$$\n\nWe now need to calculate the $y$-intercept $b.$ We can do this by substituting the coordinates of a point on the line. Any point will do, so let's substitute $(2,5):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-0.5x+b \\\\ 5 & =-0.5(2)+b \\\\ 5 & =-1+b \\\\ b & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the line is \n\n$$\ny=-0.5x+6.\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute $x=10$ into the equation above, which gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-0.5x+6 \\\\  & =-0.5(10)+6 \\\\  & =-5+6 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, according to this model, the motorcycle's value $10$ years after it was purchased is around $$1\\,000.$\n\nNote: The point where $x=10$ is not shown on our trend line. Therefore, our result *may* be unreliable." 13194139533885 true] [17592186263270 1000 #edb/ref 17592186263271 13194139533885 true] [17592186263270 1000 #edb/ref 17592186263272 13194139533885 true] [17592186263270 1000 #edb/ref 17592186263273 13194139533885 true] [17592186263270 1000 #edb/ref 17592186263274 13194139533885 true] [17592186263270 1000 #edb/ref 17592186263275 13194139533885 true] [17592186263270 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533885 true] [17592186263270 1041 "selection" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263270 1104 #edb/ref 17592186263275 13194139533885 true] [17592186263270 1110 #uuid "85615ef5-8e43-5bd3-aedd-a5b616822d65" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263271 1034 "$$1\\,500$" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263271 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533885 true] [17592186263271 1111 #uuid "d2500233-0b03-5efa-94bd-4ddb139a7774" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263272 1034 "$$2\\,250$" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263272 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533885 true] [17592186263272 1111 #uuid "a48965f3-617b-5f94-8c62-d16be7f57480" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263273 1034 "$$2\\,000$" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263273 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533885 true] [17592186263273 1111 #uuid "8f6f7c83-d69b-570b-9412-565ba9b6dd05" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263274 1034 "$$1\\,250$" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263274 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533885 true] [17592186263274 1111 #uuid "b0a63350-f208-5143-a694-b30bfe0dc5be" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263275 1034 "$$1\\,000$" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263275 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533885 true] [17592186263275 1111 #uuid "7c273700-1561-5633-9229-b381fb16844b" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263276 1017 #edb/ref 17592186263277 13194139533885 true] [17592186263276 1089 "q-133965" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263276 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139533885 true] [17592186263276 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13944892/assets/e3319694b1112e92602219492d51116d514a88e885431ac1ef0c8f8becb0dc18.png)\n\nA tea shop wants to determine the relationship between the outside temperature and the number of customers they serve. The scatter plot above shows the information they collected over several days. Assuming this trend continues, estimate the number of customers the tea shop expects to serve if the outside temperature is ${36}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}.$\n\n*Hint: Assume the trend is linear and that the trend line passes through the points $(15,60)$ and $(30,30).$*" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263276 1113 #uuid "58b0784b-138b-532b-836e-5e808016f755" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263276 1145 "First, using the hint, let's draw an approximate trend line for our scatter plot.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13944892/assets/7adb5dd9bfcfcea8842eebfcacc704237f010f87c8ffd695afab890801237abd.png)\n\nThe trend line passes through $({x}_{1},{y}_{1})=(15,60)$ and $({x}_{2},{y}_{2})=(30,30).$\n\nWe will write the equation of the line in the slope-intercept form \n\n$$\ny=mx+b.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the slope $m$ of the line as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{30-60}{30-15} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-30)}{15} \\\\  & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $m=-2$ into the slope-intercept form above, we get\n\n$$\ny=-2x+b.\n$$\n\nWe now need to calculate the $y$-intercept $b.$ We can do this by substituting the coordinates of a point on the line. Any point will do, so let's substitute $(15,60):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-2x+b \\\\ 60 & =-2(15)+b \\\\ 60 & =-30+b \\\\ b & =90\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the line is \n\n$$\ny=-2x+90.\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute $x=36$ into the equation above, which gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-2x+90 \\\\  & =-2(36)+90 \\\\  & =-72+90 \\\\  & =18.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, according to this model, the tea shop expects to serve $18$ customers.\n\nNote: The point where $x=36$ is not shown on our trend line. Therefore, our result *may* be unreliable." 13194139533885 true] [17592186263277 1000 #edb/ref 17592186263278 13194139533885 true] [17592186263277 1000 #edb/ref 17592186263279 13194139533885 true] [17592186263277 1000 #edb/ref 17592186263280 13194139533885 true] [17592186263277 1000 #edb/ref 17592186263281 13194139533885 true] [17592186263277 1000 #edb/ref 17592186263282 13194139533885 true] [17592186263277 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533885 true] [17592186263277 1041 "selection" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263277 1104 #edb/ref 17592186263282 13194139533885 true] [17592186263277 1110 #uuid "3784e314-b53b-5dcc-b4be-2301a0181239" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263278 1034 "20" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263278 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533885 true] [17592186263278 1111 #uuid "10d50e0d-996d-5c55-9617-c703ad5ef198" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263279 1034 "19" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263279 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533885 true] [17592186263279 1111 #uuid "b2ace2dd-509c-5955-ab1e-233583d1b47a" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263280 1034 "21" 13194139533885 true] [17592186263280 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533885 true] [17592186263280 1111 #uuid "670fee67-f4a1-5aad